meta {
  name: Global Search
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{BASE_URL}}/api/v1/search
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  q: lamp
  type: all
  page: 1
  page_size: 8
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # GET /api/v1/search

  Storefront search over published products and active blog posts. No token. Rate limited by `RATE_LIMIT_SEARCH` (default `120/minute`). Responses are `Cache-Control: no-store`.

  - `q`: up to 100 characters. Words are case-insensitive and can match anywhere inside a word, in any order. Every word must match (title, subtitle, category name or slug for products; title, excerpt, author, tags or body text for blogs). Letters from any script work, Bangla included. `%`, `_` and quotes are plain characters.
  - `type`: `all` (default), `products` or `blogs`. The unsearched group comes back empty.
  - `page` (1 to 1000) and `page_size` (1 to 24, default 8) apply to each group.
  - A blank `q` (or one with only punctuation) is not an error: both groups come back empty.
  - Anything invalid answers `422` with the usual `{"error": {"code", "message", "details"}}` envelope.
  - Unpublished products, products in hidden categories, inactive posts and inactive post blocks are never returned.
  - Best matches first: title matches, then subtitle and other text, then featured, then newest.

  ## Response `200`

  ```json
  {
    "query": "lamp",
    "type": "all",
    "page_size": 8,
    "products": { "items": [ /* same cards as GET /products */ ], "total": 1, "page": 1, "pages": 1 },
    "blogs": {
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "0c9a6c1e-7a55-4c0e-9f1b-5f6d8a2b3c4d",
          "slug": "choosing-a-lamp",
          "title": "Choosing a lamp",
          "excerpt": "What to look for.",
          "cover_image": "/uploads/cover.webp",
          "cover_alt": "A desk lamp",
          "author": "Mart team",
          "published_at": "3 Oct 2026",
          "read_time": "4 min",
          "tags": ["guide"]
        }
      ],
      "total": 1,
      "page": 1,
      "pages": 1
    }
  }
  ```
}

tests {
  test("returns both groups", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.products.items).to.be.an("array");
    expect(body.blogs.items).to.be.an("array");
    expect(body.page_size).to.equal(8);
  });
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 25000
}
